source_proof = "Read the actual root README, extract architecture, root RPC quickstart, transaction/receipt flow, proof, retirement and release sections, parse its curl JSON-RPC request and URL roots, and assert its topology and receipt diagram order. Trace the documented producer through rpc/send.go acceptance/forwarding, node/sequencer/accepter.go WAL release before publication, and rpc/sequencer_receipt.go committed coverage. Check the embedded host/consensus and retirement source guards, current source directories and integrated merge status."
review_only = "These are documentation source assertions, not runtime certification. Native node compilation, execution, BFT commitment, signatures, network availability, WAL durability and restart/recovery are not executed. No interface-mismatch or restart-recovery finding applies. No shell script, unit file, manifest or build file is changed or repaired; the README curl example is parsed in-process, never executed. No environment variable, credential, live endpoint, external binary, subprocess toolchain, native artifact or device is needed by pytest."
baseline = "Initial Git status/diff showed only runner-prepared .cgignore and spec task-start changes, preserved unchanged; both scoped files were absent. Private gate.json reported zero builds and verifies, and gates.jsonl did not exist. No pre-change verification was run because the explicit implementation-first order and exclusive hf-done gate prohibit a manual baseline invocation. No baseline failures are claimed."
